<title>JAPAN: Tokyo precious metal market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo precious metal market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yen-based Tokyo precious metal futures market is closed on Tuesday for a national holiday. Trading will resume on Wednesday.</p>
<p>On Monday, most-active benchmark April ended up 16 yen at 1,387 yen. Spot gold was quoted at $341.60/90 per ounce in late Asian trade, against $341.90/342.40 in New York on Friday.</p>
